{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Grid problems are rarely conceptually hard. They are **fiddly** — the difficulty is in boundaries and index arithmetic, not insight. A few habits remove most of the pain, and the problems in this chapter use all of them."
    },
